\paragraph{Single-turn transfer.}
ToxicChat jailbreaks are exclusively single-turn, while all training data consists of multi-turn conversations (5--14 turns). ToxicChat performance therefore reflects zero-shot single-turn transfer, not standard multi-turn OOD evaluation. The temporal aggregator can learn sequence length as a spurious feature: doubling the training corpus from 500 to 1{,}000 conversations drops 9-class ToxicChat macro F1 from 0.596 to [EXP17\_TOXICCHAT\_BALANCED], while multi-turn OOD detection remains stable (DD\,=\,0.889, ActorAttack\,=\,0.913). This length-dependent fragility confirms that the architecture targets multi-turn detection; single-turn robustness requires architectural changes beyond this work's scope.

\paragraph{Computation cost.}
Stage~1 continued pretraining requires approximately 30 minutes on a single A100 GPU per variant. Stage~2 training completes in under 5 minutes. Total pipeline cost for all seven variants is under 4 GPU-hours, making the approach accessible for replication.

